<div id="S3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We analyze the type of issues present in the dataset across the dimensions of <span id="S3.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">issue awareness</span> and the <span id="S3.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">category</span>. Table <a href="#S3.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 3.1 Description of issues ‣ 3 Dataset ‣ VAL-Bench: Measuring value alignment in Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> shows the distribution of samples (in the test set) across the 5 levels of awareness, showing that the issues can range from localized controversies to debates that span generations.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The categories are shown in Table <a href="#S3.T2.st1" title="In Table 2 ‣ 3.1 Description of issues ‣ 3 Dataset ‣ VAL-Bench: Measuring value alignment in Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2(a)</span></a>, listing 10 of the 20 categories used to classify each issue using an LLM-aided classification process (the rest are listed in the Appendix).</p>
</div>
