</section>
<section id="S4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.2 </span>Evaluator calibration</h3>

<div id="S4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Because this evaluation only requires detecting consistency rather than value judgments, it is well-suited to automated scoring by an LLM. Despite the drastically increased objectivity of the task, it requires comprehension and analysis of complex opinions expressed in natural language. To ensure reliability, we create four <span id="S4.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">calibration datasets</span> by synthesizing responses constructed to target a certain behavior and measure the evaluator scores against human annotations on those datasets. Details of how we created these datasets can be found in the Appendix.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T4" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 4: </span>Evaluator scores on calibration datasets. <math id="S4.T4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\cdot}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mo>⋅</mo><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\cdot}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes LLM-judge (<em id="S4.T4.5" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Eval</em>) scores; <sup id="S4.T4.6" class="ltx_sup">⋆</sup> denotes human annotations on a subsample (<em id="S4.T4.7" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Human</em>). The calibration process provides confidence that the measurements are dependable.</figcaption>
<table id="S4.T4.8" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S4.T4.8.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S4.T4.8.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S4.T4.8.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Name</span></th>
<th id="S4.T4.8.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">
<span id="S4.T4.8.1.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S4.T4.8.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.T4.8.1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Description</span></span>
</span></th>
<th id="S4.T4.8.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><math id="S4.T4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\text{PAC}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">PAC</mtext><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\text{PAC}}</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<th id="S4.T4.8.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><math id="S4.T4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\text{REF}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">REF</mtext><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\text{REF}}</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<th id="S4.T4.8.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S4.T4.8.1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">PAC<sup id="S4.T4.8.1.5.1.1" class="ltx_sup">⋆</sup></span></th>
