</figure>
<div id="A1.SS4.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">These results show that <span id="A1.SS4.SSS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">gemma-3-27B-it</span> has fairly low <span id="A1.SS4.SSS3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">PAC</span> score for the <span id="A1.SS4.SSS3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">unaligned-0</span> dataset, the highest <span id="A1.SS4.SSS3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">PAC</span> score for the <span id="A1.SS4.SSS3.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">aligned-100</span> dataset. It is also closest to measuring expected refusal rates.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.SSS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Because of this performance, we chose it as our final evaluator LLM, anditerated on the prompt to achieve calibration results shown in Table <a href="#S4.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ 4.2 Evaluator calibration ‣ 4 Evaluation ‣ VAL-Bench: Measuring value alignment in Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
</section>
